Implemented Vercel Web Analytics Configuration

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Generated updated `package-lock.json` to lock dependency versions

### 2. Code Changes
**Modified: frontend/src/app/layout.tsx**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, positioned after the `{children}` content
- Follows Next.js App Router best practices by placing the component in the root layout

## Implementation Details

The Analytics component was added following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Placed in `app/layout.tsx` (root layout file)
- Imported from `@vercel/analytics/next` (Next.js-specific package)
- Positioned inside the `<body>` element to ensure proper tracking
- Maintains existing code structure and styling

## Verification

All quality checks passed successfully:
✓ TypeScript type checking (`npm run typecheck`) - No errors
✓ Production build (`npm run build`) - Compiled successfully
✓ All pages generated correctly (7/7 static pages)
✓ No breaking changes to existing functionality
✓ Preserved existing code structure and formatting

## Next Steps

To complete the setup and start tracking analytics:
1. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard (Analytics → Select Project → Enable)
2. Deploy the application to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
3. After deployment, analytics will be automatically tracked via `/_vercel/insights/*` routes
4. Verify tracking by checking browser Network tab for requests from `/<unique-path>/view`
5. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after a few days of visitor data

## Files Changed
- frontend/package.json (added @vercel/analytics dependency)
- frontend/package-lock.json (updated with new dependencies)
